      "updated_at": "2025-06-13T20:12:17Z",
      "body": "Hi Layne,\n\nThanks for your question! Z-sem is mostly the compressed information for a group of x_0, or saying semantic variable is more accurate as it could include other things like the drug added and so on, thus z-sem is more like an embedding space for the conditions. In a simple case, if we get z_sem from x_0, and use z_sem to reconstruct x_0, yes the information is leaky, but the major task here is to learn the z-sem space, and manipulate/interpolate/extrapolate the z_sem space which could let the diffusion model generating the new data other than x_0. Hope this answer your questions!",
